  "spellcastingAbility": "cha",
  "background": "faceless",
  "backstory": "In the soot-choked alleys of a city that never learned his name, a child of infernal blood was forged in the fires of survival. Born with the tell-tale horns and vibrant skin of the tiefling race, he was a marked soul from his first breath, an easy target for the superstitions and cruelty of a world that fears what it does not understand. To endure, he mastered the art of the blade not out of a sense of knightly duty, but out of a desperate necessity to carve a path through the grasping hands of those who would see him chained. He became a student of steel, a fighter who found more comfort in the cold weight of a longsword than in the warmth of a hearth. His martial prowess is a silent language, refined through years of skirmishes where the only law was to strike fast and remain a shadow.\n\nThe mask he wears is more than a simple disguise; it is his true face, a vessel of absolute liberation. Behind the lacquered wood and the deep cowl, he is no longer a cursed pariah, but a phantom of the road—a nameless spirit who answers to no master and owes no debts. This dual existence is his most sacred bond, for he knows that if the world were to see the man beneath the iron and leather, his hard-won liberty would vanish like smoke. He wanders the realms as a free agent of chaos, taking up the call of adventure primarily because the movement keeps his secrets buried and his trail cold. Yet, for all his skill, he is a survivor at heart; he carries no illusions of martyrdom. If a battle turns sour or a conversation probes too deeply into the man behind the mask, he is gone before the dust settles, always seeking the next horizon where he can remain a mystery.",
